    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><div dir=\"auto\">I think the error is saying that you’ve missed a step. </div></div><div dir=\"auto\"><br></div><div dir=\"auto\">!! (Bang bang) is expecting a symbol so you need to make your input variables symbols with  rlang::sym(). </div></div><div><div dir=\"auto\"><br></div>err_plot = function(lstat, medv) {<br></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div>lstat &lt;-  sym(lstat)</div><div>medv &lt;- sym(medv)</div><div><br></div><div>qplot(!!lstat, !!medv)</div></blockquote><div>}<br><div><br></div><div>My favorite tutorial for tidy evaluation is here:</div><div><a href=\"https://edwinth.github.io/blog/dplyr-recipes/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://edwinth.github.io/blog/dplyr-recipes/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366358574000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1DEUzI-96yVp1JiNKjsref\">https://edwinth.github.io/blog/dplyr-recipes/</a></div><div><br></div><div>I know that Hadley has also updated his Advanced R book. </div><div><a href=\"https://adv-r.hadley.nz/quasiquotation.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://adv-r.hadley.nz/quasiquotation.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366358574000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1-axZjA-rbDkqScQVr1dtw\">https://adv-r.hadley.nz/quasiquotation.html</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>HTH, </div><div>B</div><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
