     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div dir=\"ltr\">I remembered something like this too, but I don&#39;t see anything in the recent release notes to indicate that this is the case. <div><a href=\"https://github.com/tidyverse/ggplot2/releases\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/tidyverse/ggplot2/releases&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366358583000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2OZycTdpFH5opYMjjIHf_8\">https://github.com/tidyverse/ggplot2/releases</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>Also, it does still work. </div><div><br></div><div>library(ggplot2)</div><div>qplot(mtcars$hp, mtcars$disp)<br></div><div><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2/attach/1bd9e80b5f6d5a/Screen%20Shot%202019-01-24%20at%203.26.32%20PM.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"Screen Shot 2019-01-24 at 3.26.32 PM.png\" width=\"188\" height=\"172\" style=\"margin-right:0px\"><br></div><div><br></div><div>B</div><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
